MozJPEG includes libjpeg-turbo under the compatible IJG, modified BSD, and
zlib licenses. The required IJG notice is in README.ijg; the license roll-up
and BSD/zlib terms are in LICENSE.md.

The Wasm encoder is built from the verified archive with the repository's
scripts/mozjpeg/build.sh and scripts/mozjpeg/encoder.c. The small source patch
mem-dest-owner.patch updates jpeg_mem_dest's caller-owned pointer after each
successful output-buffer growth, so a later longjmp can free the current
allocation. It also provides cleanup for progressive scan buffers on success
and error, and restores standard Huffman tables after trellis analysis when
baseline output requests non-optimized Huffman coding.

The build is single-threaded, enables WebAssembly SIMD with -msimd128, and
disables arithmetic coding, 12-bit samples, PNG, TurboJPEG, Java and tools.
Only the static JPEG library objects referenced by the RGBA compressor are
linked. Memory growth is enabled with a 1 GiB maximum.
