Security review
The upstream MozJPEG 4.1.5 ChangeLog and NVD entries were reviewed against the
linked path. The archive includes fixes for encoder and decoder issues listed
there. Image decoding is done by the browser; this Wasm module receives RGBA
pixels and contains no JPEG decoder, command-line reader, PPM/BMP/GIF loader,
arithmetic coder, lossless transformer or TurboJPEG API. PNG and TurboJPEG are
disabled, which excludes the indexed-PNG tj3LoadImage* division-by-zero
described by CVE-2026-75466.

